.nh
.TH "AUTOSNAP" "1" "Aug 2026" "autosnap" "autosnap manual"

.SH NAME
autosnap-mark - Mark checkpoints with an arbitrary label


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBautosnap mark (--label LABEL|--bad|--good|--review|--unmark)  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Mark one checkpoint or an inclusive checkpoint range with an arbitrary label.

.PP
A range A..B marks checkpoints from A through B, inclusive. Ranges are
inclusive autosnap checkpoint intervals, not general Git revision ranges.

.PP
Labels must be 1-32 characters matching [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_-]*. The label
unmarked is reserved. Use --reason with --label or --bad to record why a
checkpoint was marked.

.PP
The checkpoint argument can be an explicit autosnap ref, a checkpoint commit hash,
or one of these current-branch history selectors:

.PP
first
  first+N
  last
  last-N


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--bad\fP[=false]
	Mark selected checkpoints bad

.PP
\fB--good\fP[=false]
	Mark selected checkpoints good

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for mark

.PP
\fB--label\fP=""
	Arbitrary mark label

.PP
\fB--reason\fP=""
	Human-readable reason for the mark

.PP
\fB--review\fP[=false]
	Mark selected checkpoints for review

.PP
\fB--unmark\fP[=false]
	Remove explicit review, good, or bad marks from selected checkpoints


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBautosnap(1)\fP
